Finding: {"title":"curriculum-export routes take the full curriculum payload from the request body with no ownership/tenant check","severity":"LOW","area":"Authorization boundary","files":["src/server/routes/routes-curriculum-export.ts"],"detail":"POST /curriculum-export/generate and POST /curriculum-export/revise-page both accept an arbitrary `curriculum`/`module` object directly in the request body (lines 289-302, 566-584) and never look it up by ID against the DB scoped to `orgId` — they only call `requireAuth()` plus a best-effort `resolveOrgIdFromSession` used solely for token-usage attribution, not authorization. Any authenticated user (any org) can submit any curriculum shape they construct client-side and get it converted through Claude into an export document.","impact":"Low real-world impact since the caller already possesses/constructs the full curriculum content in the request — no cross-tenant data is exfiltrated that the caller didn't already have. But it does mean these two endpoints provide unmetered/unrestricted AI generation to any authenticated user regardless of which org's curriculum data they submit, and token usage is billed to whatever orgId the caller happens to resolve to rather than being enforced against a curriculum record's actual owning org.","recommendation":"If curriculum export is meant to be scoped per-org/per-curriculum-record, look the curriculum up by ID + orgId server-side rather than trusting the client-submitted object wholesale. If the current design (client sends full object) is intentional (e.g. for previewing unsaved edits), document that decision explicitly.","confidence":"low"}
confirmed=true only if the defect genuinely exists. If misread → verdict="false-positive". If real but wrong severity → set correctedSeverity. If real but underspecified → verdict="needs-detail" (kept). Return JSON per the schema.

